urname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><surname>Barraclough</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudland</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Induction of the metastatic phenotype by transfection of a benign rat mammary epithelial cell line with the gene for p9Ka, a rat calcium-binding protein, but not with the oncogene EJ-ras-1</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1993</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>999</fpage><lpage>1008</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncogene||8|999||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8455951</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitano</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikenaka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shirasaka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of coadministration of uracil or cytosine on the anti-tumor activity of clinical doses of 1-(2-tetrahydrofuryl)-5 fluorouracil and level of 5 &#x02013; fluorouracil in rodents</article-title><source>Gann</source><year>1979</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>209</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Gann||70|209||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">381088</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garrett</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Varney</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bresnick</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>S100A4, a mediator of metastasis</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2006</year><volume>281</volume><fpage>677</fpage><lpage>680</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||281|6